<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qifu Guoren</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 388</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qifu Guoren was a chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qifu-clan">Qifu clan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> who founded Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> in 385, after the collapse of Former Qin following the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fei-river">Battle of Fei River</a>. He ruled from Yuanchuan near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhongyong-of-wu">Yuzhong</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> over Xianbei herders and Chinese farmers, and was succeeded by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qifu-gangui">Qifu Gangui</a> in 388.</p></div>
